## Slot vocabulary ({{slot-count}} slots inherited or declared)

Observation memorials inherit `:mm/Memory` plus class-specific extensions:

- **`:mm.observation/confidence`** — `:tentative` / `:likely` / `:certain` — how sure are we?
- **`:mm.observation/scale-dependent`** — true if relevance grows with system scale (O(n²), context-budget pressure, table-size thresholds)
- **`evidence`** — supporting measurements, code references, incidents

{{slot-table}}

## Canonical body structure

```markdown
## The observation

<One paragraph — what was noticed.  Be specific.>

## How it was noticed

<Context — what session / work / event surfaced this.>

## Implications

<Why a future session would want to know this.  Zero or more
concrete consequences.>

## Evidence

<What supports the observation (measurements, code references,
incidents).  Distinguishes `tentative` from `certain`.>

## Related observations / work

<Adjacent memorials — patterns it might extend, bugs it might
explain, ideas it might justify.>
```

## Lifecycle

Observations are generally write-once-then-graduate:

- **Validated** — confidence bumps (`tentative` → `likely` → `certain`); update `last-reviewed`
- **Invalidated** — don't delete; add a `## Invalidation` section noting what falsified it.  Forensic trail matters
- **Graduated** — when an observation develops into a formal anti-pattern, pattern, or bug, link forward to the successor; keep the observation

## Pitfalls

- **Observations as hidden ideas** — if every observation ends with *"we should fix this,"* it's an idea, not an observation
- **Observation inflation** — writing 20 observations per session erodes signal; reserve for things a future session would genuinely benefit from
- **Confidence inflation** — marking things `certain` when they're really `likely`; trust-erosion risk when a `certain` observation turns out wrong

## State-change-detection (captureability)

This class is mid-conversation-captureable.  Inject-triggers:
- *"huh, didn't expect..."*
- *"turns out..."*
- *"I noticed..."*

When these signals fire, capture-first: write an observation memorial with the body shape above, then proceed.

## Composition with adjacent classes

- **`question`** — observations are statements; questions are gaps.  A question may resolve into an observation
- **`idea`** — observations may motivate ideas (proposed action based on noticed truth)
- **`pattern`** / **`anti-pattern`** — observations accumulating around a shape may graduate to named convention
- **`plan`** — observations frequently appear in plan §0 (motivation) or `## Retrospective`

